{
 "thread": "HRyQbbWE7v8",
 "subject": "Multiple-group confirmatory factor analysis - can't find difftest()",
 "messages_listed": 4,
 "last_activity": "2018-11-23T15:53:01Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "OLuGNEQiBgAJ",
   "from": "Matti Cervin",
   "author": "599ef5398c0eeef8",
   "date": "2018-08-22T07:46:33Z",
   "subject": "Multiple-group confirmatory factor analysis - can't find difftest()",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;.SFNSText-Regular&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(29,33,41);font-size:14px\">I am performing a multiple-group confirmatory factor analysis in lavaan for a paper I am working on, guided by this tutorial: <a href=\"https://pareonline.net/pdf/v19n7.pdf\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(54,88,153);font-family:inherit\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://pareonline.net/pdf/v19n7.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792424527879000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2_eFiV519G5bs6t3wuDbq0\">https://pareonline.net/pdf/v19n7.pdf</a>.</p><p style=\"font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;.SFNSText-Regular&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(29,33,41);font-size:14px\"><br></p><p style=\"font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;.SFNSText-Regular&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(29,33,41);font-size:14px\">I work with ordinal indicators and when I try to run the semTools:::difftest(), I get this warning message:</p><p style=\"font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;.SFNSText-Regular&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(29,33,41);font-size:14px\"><br></p><p style=\"font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;.SFNSText-Regular&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(29,33,41);font-size:14px\">Error in get(name, envir = asNamespace(pkg), inherits = FALSE) : <br>object &#39;difftest&#39; not found</p><div><p style=\"display:inline;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;.SFNSText-Regular&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(29,33,41);font-size:14px\"><br></p></div><div><p style=\"display:inline;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;.SFNSText-Regular&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(29,33,41);font-size:14px\">This is the code:</p></div><div><p style=\"display:inline;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;.SFNSText-Regular&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(29,33,41);font-size:14px\"><br></p></div><div><div><font color=\"#1d2129\" face=\"system-ui, -apple-system, system-ui, .SFNSText-Regular, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>config &lt;- cfa(original_model, estimator=&quot;WLSMV&quot;,data=mg_cfa_gr_ord, group=&quot;identifier&quot;,</i></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1d2129\" face=\"system-ui, -apple-system, system-ui, .SFNSText-Regular, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>               ordered = c(&quot;o1&quot;,&quot;o2&quot;,&quot;o3&quot;,&quot;o4&quot;,&quot;o5&quot;,&quot;o6&quot;, &quot;o7&quot;, &quot;o8&quot;, &quot;o9&quot;,</i></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1d2129\" face=\"system-ui, -apple-system, system-ui, .SFNSText-Regular, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>                           &quot;o10&quot;,&quot;o11&quot;,&quot;o12&quot;,&quot;o13&quot;,&quot;o14&quot;,&quot;o15&quot;,&quot;o16&quot;,&quot;o17&quot;,</i></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1d2129\" face=\"system-ui, -apple-system, system-ui, .SFNSText-Regular, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>                           &quot;o18&quot;,&quot;o19&quot;,&quot;o20&quot;,&quot;o21&quot;))</i></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1d2129\" face=\"system-ui, -apple-system, system-ui, .SFNSText-Regular, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><br></i></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1d2129\" face=\"system-ui, -apple-system, system-ui, .SFNSText-Regular, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>weak &lt;- cfa(original_model, estimator=&quot;WLSMV&quot;, data=mg_cfa_gr_ord,</i></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1d2129\" face=\"system-ui, -apple-system, system-ui, .SFNSText-Regular, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>             ordered = c(&quot;o1&quot;,&quot;o2&quot;,&quot;o3&quot;,&quot;o4&quot;,&quot;o5&quot;,&quot;o6&quot;, &quot;o7&quot;, &quot;o8&quot;, &quot;o9&quot;,</i></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1d2129\" face=\"system-ui, -apple-system, system-ui, .SFNSText-Regular, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>                         &quot;o10&quot;,&quot;o11&quot;,&quot;o12&quot;,&quot;o13&quot;,&quot;o14&quot;,&quot;o15&quot;,&quot;o16&quot;,&quot;o17&quot;,</i></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1d2129\" face=\"system-ui, -apple-system, system-ui, .SFNSText-Regular, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>                         &quot;o18&quot;,&quot;o19&quot;,&quot;o20&quot;,&quot;o21&quot;),</i></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1d2129\" face=\"system-ui, -apple-system, system-ui, .SFNSText-Regular, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>            group=&quot;identifier&quot;, group.equal = c(&quot;loadings&quot;))</i></span></font></div></div><div><font color=\"#1d2129\" face=\"system-ui, -apple-system, system-ui, .SFNSText-Regular, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><br></i></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>semTools::difftest(config,weak)</i></span><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><br></i></span></font></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(29,33,41);font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;.SFNSText-Regular&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Does this mean that the difftest() function is not longer included in the semTools package? Does anyone know which function to use instead?</span><font color=\"#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><br></i></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br></span></font></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "0On6lxgcBwAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2018-08-25T12:04:43Z",
   "subject": "Re: Multiple-group confirmatory factor analysis - can't find difftest()",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(29,33,41);font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;.SFNSText-Regular&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Does this mean that the difftest() function is not longer included in the semTools package? </span></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>It never was a function offered by the semTools package.  Notice the three colons between semTools and difftest?  That indicates it is a hidden/private function used only internally.  The paper you are using unfortunately was very irresponsible in providing guidance that relied on something that was volatile.  It ceased to exist a few versions ago</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(29,33,41);font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;.SFNSText-Regular&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Does anyone know which function to use instead?</span></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>See the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> ?lavTestLRT </font>help page.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792424527880000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2o8k4-rlR0vH2dnTg4EAOP\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "75XYpqkPAgAJ",
   "from": "Hui Zhang",
   "author": "5b5825f096cf5569",
   "date": "2018-11-19T06:54:58Z",
   "subject": "Re: Multiple-group confirmatory factor analysis - can't find difftest()",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I would like to ask a follow up question; I referred to the same paper that Matti Cervin referred to.  I looked up lavTestLRT and tried to replicate the results in the same paper.</div><div><br></div><div>I used this syntax:</div><div><br></div><div>lavTestLRT(scs_model_config,scs_model_weak,A.method=&quot;delta&quot;,type=&quot;Chisq&quot;)<br></div><div><br></div><div>and would like to ask whether it is correct and if it is, why no AIC or BIC are reported, I got</div><div><br></div><div><div>                 Df AIC BIC  Chisq Chisq diff Df diff Pr(&gt;Chisq)    </div><div>scs_model_config 70         1135.1                                  </div><div>scs_model_weak   79         1310.9     81.827       9  7.003e-14 ***</div></div><div><br></div><div>The authors of the paper reported delta.cfi.</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you!</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br>On Saturday, August 25, 2018 at 8:04:43 AM UTC-4, Terrence Jorgensen wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(29,33,41);font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;.SFNSText-Regular&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Does this mean that the difftest() function is not longer included in the semTools package? </span></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>It never was a function offered by the semTools package.  Notice the three colons between semTools and difftest?  That indicates it is a hidden/private function used only internally.  The paper you are using unfortunately was very irresponsible in providing guidance that relied on something that was volatile.  It ceased to exist a few versions ago</div><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(29,33,41);font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;.SFNSText-Regular&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Does anyone know which function to use instead?</span></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>See the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> ?lavTestLRT </font>help page.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792424527882000&amp;usg=AOvVaw36xMCkexYjP1BlTYc01H4R\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "nGgb7yx2BgAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2018-11-23T15:53:01Z",
   "subject": "Re: Multiple-group confirmatory factor analysis - can't find difftest()",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p><div><p></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>lavTestLRT(scs_model_config,scs_model_weak,A.method=&quot;delta&quot;,type=&quot;Chisq&quot;)<br></div><div><br></div><div>and would like to ask whether it is correct</div></div></blockquote><p></p></div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">What, the syntax?  Yes.</p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p><div><p></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div> and if it is, why no AIC or BIC are reported, <br></div><div></div></div></blockquote><p></p></div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">If you used a least-squares estimator (e.g., DWLS for categorical outcomes) instead of a likelihood estimator, then there is no likelihood with which to calculate information criteria.</p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p><div><p></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The authors of the paper reported delta.cfi.</div></div></blockquote><p></p></div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">That will not tell you anything useful, but you can find the CFI from each model using <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">fitMeasures()</code>.  You can also use the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">compareFit()</code> function in semTools.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Terrence D. Jorgensen<br>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"><br>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam<br></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792424527885000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0zOH075cO0vGJGaQPT94Dj\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGJsb2NrcXVvdGUgY2xhc3M9ImdtYWlsX3F1b3RlIiBzdHlsZT0ibWFyZ2luOiAwO21hcmdpbi1s\r\nZWZ0OiAwLjhleDtib3JkZXItbGVmdDogMXB4ICNjY2Mgc29saWQ7cGFkZGluZy1sZWZ0OiAxZXg7\r\nIj48ZGl2IGRpcj0ibHRyIj48ZGl2PmxhdlRlc3RMUlQoc2NzX21vZGVsX2NvbmZpZyw8d2JyPnNj\r\nc19tb2RlbF93ZWFrLEEubWV0aG9kPSI8d2JyPmRlbHRhIix0eXBlPSJDaGlzcSIpPGJyPjwvZGl2\r\nPjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+YW5kIHdvdWxkIGxpa2UgdG8gYXNrIHdoZXRoZXIgaXQgaXMg\r\nY29ycmVjdDwvZGl2PjwvZGl2PjwvYmxvY2txdW90ZT48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PldoYXQs\r\nIHRoZSBzeW50YXg/Jm5ic3A7IFllcy48L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48YmxvY2txdW90ZSBj\r\nbGFzcz0iZ21haWxfcXVvdGUiIHN0eWxlPSJtYXJnaW46IDA7bWFyZ2luLWxlZnQ6IDAuOGV4O2Jv\r\ncmRlci1sZWZ0OiAxcHggI2NjYyBzb2xpZDtwYWRkaW5nLWxlZnQ6IDFleDsiPjxkaXYgZGlyPSJs\r\ndHIiPjxkaXY+IGFuZCBpZiBpdCBpcywgd2h5IG5vIEFJQyBvciBCSUMgYXJlIHJlcG9ydGVkLCA8\r\nYnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj48L2Rpdj48L2Rpdj48L2Jsb2NrcXVvdGU+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRp\r\ndj5JZiB5b3UgdXNlZCBhIGxlYXN0LXNxdWFyZXMgZXN0aW1hdG9yIChlLmcuLCBEV0xTIGZvciBj\r\nYXRlZ29yaWNhbCBvdXRjb21lcykgaW5zdGVhZCBvZiBhIGxpa2VsaWhvb2QgZXN0aW1hdG9yLCB0\r\naGVuIHRoZXJlIGlzIG5vIGxpa2VsaWhvb2Qgd2l0aCB3aGljaCB0byBjYWxjdWxhdGUgaW5mb3Jt\r\nYXRpb24gY3JpdGVyaWEuPC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGJsb2NrcXVvdGUgY2xhc3M9Imdt\r\nYWlsX3F1b3RlIiBzdHlsZT0ibWFyZ2luOiAwO21hcmdpbi1sZWZ0OiAwLjhleDtib3JkZXItbGVm\r\ndDogMXB4ICNjY2Mgc29saWQ7cGFkZGluZy1sZWZ0OiAxZXg7Ij48ZGl2IGRpcj0ibHRyIj48ZGl2\r\nPlRoZSBhdXRob3JzIG9mIHRoZSBwYXBlciByZXBvcnRlZCBkZWx0YS5jZmkuPC9kaXY+PC9kaXY+\r\nPC9ibG9ja3F1b3RlPjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+VGhhdCB3aWxsIG5vdCB0ZWxsIHlvdSBh\r\nbnl0aGluZyB1c2VmdWwsIGJ1dCB5b3UgY2FuIGZpbmQgdGhlIENGSSBmcm9tIGVhY2g